* {{a|US|Canada}} {{IPA|en|/nuˈmoʊniə/|/nəˈmoʊniə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s|pneumoniæ}}

# An acute or chronic inflammation of the lungs caused by [[virus]]es, [[bacterium|bacteria]] or other [[microorganism]]s, or sometimes by physical or chemical [[irritant]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=[[w:Michael Arlen|Michael Arlen]]|title=“Piracy”: A Romantic Chronicle of These Days|chapter=2/9/1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1519647W|passage=He had always been remarkably immune from such little ailments, and had only once in his life been ill, of a vicious '''pneumonia''' long ago at school.}}

